---
title: Book it without a mouse
order: 3
summary: Push the mouse away. Find out how much of an interface simply is not there when you can only use a keyboard.
scenario: You have your arm in a sling for six weeks. You can type, slowly, with one hand. You cannot hold a mouse. You need to book a meeting room for tomorrow morning before somebody else takes it.
tasks:
  - Move your mouse and trackpad out of reach. No touching, no cheating.
  - Using Tab, Shift and Tab, Enter and the space bar only, book the Ceredigion room at 10:00 and ask for the video kit.
  - When you get stuck, press the button that counts what a keyboard can actually reach.
time: 10 minutes
barrier: Controls that are not controls, and focus you cannot see
criterion: WCAG 2.2 &mdash; <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/keyboard.html">2.1.1 Keyboard</a> and <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/focus-visible.html">2.4.7 Focus Visible</a>
script: keyboard.js
---

